USBPcap - USB Packet capture for Windows

End-user installer is available at: http://desowin.org/usbpcap
Following informations are intended for developers and power users only.

Directory overview:
  USBPcapCMD - sample user space application
  USBPcapDriver - filter driver used to capture data

Build instructions (Windows Server 2025):
  Install Visual Studio 2026 with the Desktop development with C++ workload,
  the Windows Driver Kit individual component, and the Spectre-mitigated
  libraries. Then install the matching current Windows SDK and Windows Driver
  Kit (WDK 10.0.28000, the Windows 11 version 26H1 kit). The latest WDK builds
  drivers for Windows Server 2025 and for older supported releases.

  From this directory run:
    build_server2025.bat

  That builds USBPcap.sys and USBPcapCMD.exe for x64 and ARM64 with
  NTDDI_WIN11_GE (Windows 11 24H2 / Windows Server 2025, build 26100) and
  writes packages to:
    Release\Server2025\x64
    Release\Server2025\ARM64

  Open USBPcap.sln in Visual Studio 2026 to build Debug or Release from the IDE.
  The kernel project uses the WindowsKernelModeDriver10.0 toolset.

  Windows Server 2025 has no x86 kernel. The driver allocates nonpaged pool
  with ExAllocatePool2 so it can load when hypervisor-enforced code integrity
  is turned on.

  The driver_build*.bat scripts still describe the Windows 7.1 DDK and the
  Windows 8.1 WDK. Those kits are not how this tree is built for Server 2025.

Installation:
  The packages produced by build_server2025.bat are not attestation signed.
  To load one on a 64-bit machine, enable test signing and reboot:
    Bcdedit.exe -set TESTSIGNING ON

  Right click on the USBPcap.inf file and select Install.

  After installing, reboot.

  A catalog built for Server2025_X64 or Server2025_ARM64 does not replace a
  Microsoft attestation signature. Production installs need an EV-signed
  submission to the Hardware Dev Center.

Usage:
  Currently there is no capture engine dll.
  You can use the USBPcapCMD.exe to select the filter instance (there is one
  instance per root hub) and specify the output pcap file name.

Licensing:
  USBPcapDriver is licensed under GPLv2 license.
  USBPcapCMD is licensed under BSD 2-Clause license.

